c Stack and Queue)\n     - Stage 6: Recursion and backtracking. (Topics: Recursion, Backtracking)\n     - Stage 7: Trees and binary search trees. (Topics: Trees and Binary Trees, Binary Search Trees, Tries)\n     - Stage 8: Heaps and graphs. (Topics: Heaps and Priority Queues, Graphs, Breadth-First Search (BFS), Depth-First Search (DFS), Topological Sorting, Union-Find)\n     - Stage 9: Greedy algorithms and dynamic programming. (Topics: Greedy Algorithms, Dynamic Programming, Intervals)\n     - Stage 10: Advanced patterns and data structures. (Topics: Advanced Data Structures, Bit Manipulation, Math and Number Theory, Matrix Problems)\n   - Real completion rules:\n     - A stage should compute its total problems, solved count, attempted count, and mastery status dynamically from `this.progress.solved` and `this.progress.attempted`.\n     - Stage status:\n       - `Mastered`: >= 60% solved or all milestone problems completed.\n       - `In Progress`: at least 1 problem solved or attempted.\n       - `Not Started`: 0 solved and 0 attempted.\n     - Each stage should render:\n       - Stage number, title, description, and topics chips.\n       - Progress bar with percentage and `X/Y Solved`.\n       - Milestone problem card with direct button to `openProblemWorkspace(milestoneId)`.\n       - List of featured practice problems with their actual status badges.\n       - \"Practice Next\" button pointing to the first unsolved problem in that stage.\n       - \"Explore All Stage Problems\" button which sets `selectedTopic` or filters to that stage's topics and switches to problem table.\n       - Stage selector button to set \"Active Learning Stage\" stored in `localStorage` under `dsa_active_stage`.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes (Exhaustive History)**\n   - *PowerShell Quoting/Interpolation with inline python/node*: PowerShell fails with double quotes inside `-c` or string redirection `<`. Workaround: Always write `.py` or `.js` scripts into `scratch/` and execute via file path